  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Privacy policy</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_Updated" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Last updated: November 25, 2026</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_1_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>In short</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_1_Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>SophiApp for Windows does not collect, store, sell, or share your personal data. The app has no user accounts, telemetry, analytics, or advertising, and Team Sophia has no servers that receive data from it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_2_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>What stays on your PC</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_2_Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The app keeps two things in its own folder: the `Settings.json` file with the app settings (window size and position, theme, language, the notes you closed, and the fact that you accepted these terms) and the `Log` folder with a log of what the app checked and changed. The log contains the names of your PC and your user account, your Windows version, and the settings you applied. These files never leave your PC unless you send them to us yourself, and you can delete them at any time.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_3_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Connections the app makes</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_3_Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>At every start and when you install something, the app connects to third-party servers: GitHub, to check for new versions of the app and of the components it installs, to get the lists of supported Windows builds and Linux distributions, and to download the cursors; Microsoft, to download the installers you chose, such as .NET, Visual C++, OneDrive, and WSL; and the DNS-over-HTTPS provider you chose, to make sure its server responds. Windows features that the app starts, such as Windows Update, connect to Microsoft in their usual way. As with any Internet connection, these servers see your IP address and the technical details of the request. The app sends them no information about you, your PC, or your settings. Each company handles this data under its own privacy policy.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_4_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Links</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_4_Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The links to GitHub, Telegram, Discord, Microsoft, and other sites open in your browser. Those sites have their own privacy policies.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_5_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When you contact us</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_5_Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>If you report a problem on GitHub, in Telegram, or in Discord, we see what you post there, including the log file if you attach it. We use it only to solve the problem. Look through the log before you share it. Those platforms handle your account data under their own policies.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_6_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>European Union, EEA, and United Kingdom</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_6_Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The app does not send your personal data to us, so Team Sophia does not act as a controller of your personal data under the GDPR and the UK GDPR while you use the app. If you have sent us something and want it removed, write to us and we will delete what we control. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with your data protection authority.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_7_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>United States</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_7_Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>We do not sell or share personal information and do not use it for targeted advertising or profiling, as these terms are defined by the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) and similar state laws.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_8_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Canada</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_8_Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>We do not collect, use, or disclose personal information through the app within the meaning of the Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act (PIPEDA) and Quebec's Law 25.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_9_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Children</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_9_Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The app is a tool for administrators of Windows PCs and is not directed to children. We do not knowingly collect data from anyone, including children.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_10_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Changes and contact</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrivacyPolicy_10_Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When this policy changes, the date above is updated, and the app asks you to accept the new version at the next start. Questions about this policy: [GitHub]({0}) or [Telegram]({1}).</value>
  </data>
