  <data name="TaskSchedulerPage_AboutTasks.Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The scheduled tasks below are sufficient to keep Windows clean. There is no need to constantly clean other system folders, as is often advised on the Internet. The tasks respect the **Do not disturb** mode: their notifications won't pop up while you are playing a game, watching a video in full screen, or when the mode is turned on.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TaskSchedulerPage_OpenTaskScheduler.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Open Task Scheduler</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_CleanupTask_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create Windows Cleanup scheduled task</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_CleanupTask_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create the "Windows Cleanup" task and the "Windows Cleanup Notification" task, which shows a pop-up notification, in the Sophia folder of Task Scheduler to clean up unused files and Windows updates. Every 30 days a native notification prompts you to run the cleanup, and another one appears when it completes.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TaskScheduler_WindowsCleanup_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cleaning up unused Windows files and updates using the built-in Disk Cleanup app. The scheduled task can run only if the user "{0}" is signed in.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TaskScheduler_WindowsCleanupNotification_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A pop-up notification reminder about cleaning up unused Windows files and updates. The scheduled task can run only if the user "{0}" is signed in.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TaskScheduler_WindowsCleanupToast_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Windows cleanup</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TaskScheduler_WindowsCleanupToast_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Run the task to clean up unused Windows files and updates?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TaskScheduler_WindowsCleanupToast_Run" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Run</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_SoftwareDistributionTask_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create SoftwareDistribution scheduled task</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_SoftwareDistributionTask_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create the "SoftwareDistribution" task in the Sophia folder of Task Scheduler to clean up the `%SystemRoot%\SoftwareDistribution\Download` folder, where Windows update installation files are downloaded. The task waits until the Windows Update service has finished running. It runs every 90 days and shows a native Windows notification when it completes.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TaskScheduler_SoftwareDistribution_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cleaning up the Windows update cache folder "{1}". The scheduled task can run only if the user "{0}" is signed in.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TaskScheduler_SoftwareDistributionToast_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The Windows update cache was successfully deleted.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_TempTask_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create Temp scheduled task</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_TempTask_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create the "Temp" task in the Sophia folder of Task Scheduler to clean up the `%TEMP%` folder. Only files older than one day are deleted. The task runs every 60 days and shows a native Windows notification when it completes.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TaskScheduler_TempTask_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cleaning up the temporary folder "{1}" (%TEMP%). The scheduled task can run only if the user "{0}" is signed in.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TaskScheduler_TempTaskToast_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The temporary folder was successfully cleaned up.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_NetworkProtection_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable Microsoft Defender Exploit Guard network protection</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_NetworkProtection_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Network protection helps prevent users from using any application to access dangerous domains that may host phishing scams, exploits, and other malicious content on the Internet.</value>
  </data>
